# Options for cenziadah-watch.service (cenziadah watch --json $CENZIADAH_ARGS).
# After editing: systemctl restart cenziadah-watch
#
# Common options:
#   --interval 10s            idle time between the end of a sweep and the next
#   --pace 1ms                pause after each process within a sweep (0 = none)
#   --mail-to ADDR            e-mail new alerts (and a startup summary) to ADDR
#                             through the local sendmail (an MTA must be installed)
#   --mail-min medium         lowest severity mailed: low|medium|high|critical
#   --mail-max-per-hour 20    rate limit for alert mails (the journal keeps everything)
#   --sendmail PATH           sendmail program (default /usr/sbin/sendmail); must be
#                             root-owned and not writable by others
#   --mail-from ADDR          From address (default: the MTA's configured sender)
#   --no-auto-learn           do not learn programs first seen after start
#   --skip-exe PATH=REASON    do not inspect an executable (reason is reported)
#
# Example (ALL options inside ONE pair of quotes):
#   CENZIADAH_ARGS="--interval 10s --mail-to ops@example.com"
# Check before restarting:
#   cenziadah watch --check-config --interval 10s --mail-to ops@example.com
CENZIADAH_ARGS="--interval 10s"
